ai-title = AI assistant
ai-intro = Describe a part or attach a photo or dimensioned drawing. Check the preview before adding it.
ai-settings = API connection
ai-endpoint = Full chat/completions URL
ai-model = Model ID
ai-key = API key (optional for a local server)
ai-key-session = Connection settings and the key are kept only until the program closes.
ai-http = HTTP is not encrypted. Use it only with a trusted local server; use HTTPS for a remote service.
ai-prompt = Part description or revision
ai-example = Open-top housing 150 x 100 x 60 mm, wall and floor 3 mm.
ai-sent = The description, current images and last six turns are sent to the service. Attached images are sent with each request until removed. Other project geometry is not sent.
ai-send = Generate preview
ai-wait = Generating and checking geometry...
ai-cancel = Discard request
ai-cancelled = The result will be discarded. A request already sent may still be processed by the service.
ai-clear = Start a new conversation
ai-variant = Each addition creates a new part. Revisions create a new variant and keep the previous part.
ai-apply = Add part
ai-finish-edit = Finish or cancel the current modelling command before adding the part.
ai-operations = Construction operations
ai-preview-drag = Drag horizontally to rotate the preview.
ai-undo = Add AI part
ai-inserted = The part was added. Undo removes it in one step.
ai-error-insert = The part could not be inserted. Open a project and try again.
ai-error-plan = The recipe is empty or exceeds 48 operations. Request a simpler part.
ai-error-range = Dimensions must be 0.05 to 2000 mm and translations no more than 2000 mm. Specify smaller values.
ai-error-reference = A body reference is missing, duplicated or already consumed. Request a corrected recipe.
ai-error-one-body = Separate bodies remain. Request one connected part.
ai-error-geometry = The shape could not be built as one valid solid. Simplify the part or reduce the fillet radius.
ai-error-reply = The service returned an incomplete or unsupported recipe. Use a model that follows JSON instructions and try again.
ai-error-settings = Enter the full HTTP(S) chat/completions URL and model ID. Put the key only in the key field.
ai-error-prompt = Enter a description of at most 12000 bytes.
ai-error-auth = Access was refused. Check the API key and model permissions.
ai-error-quota = The service limit was reached. Check the quota or try later.
ai-error-server = The service refused the request. Check the address, model ID and chat/completions compatibility.
ai-error-network = The connection failed or the service did not respond in 120 seconds. Check the address, network and certificate.
ai-error-worker = Generation stopped unexpectedly. Try a simpler request.
ai-op-box = Box
ai-op-cylinder = Cylinder
ai-op-sphere = Sphere
ai-op-move = Move
ai-op-cut = Cut
ai-op-union = Union
ai-op-intersect = Intersect
ai-op-fillet = Fillet all edges
ai-history = Conversation history
ai-add-image = Attach photo or drawing
ai-image-formats = Photos and drawings
ai-image-loading = Loading image...
ai-vision-hint = Requires a model that accepts images. Keep dimensions legible; specify any missing thickness or scale.
ai-images-attached = Attached images ({ $count })
ai-remove-image = Remove image
ai-image-prompt-default = Create one mechanical part from the attached images and written dimensions. Ask for any missing measurements before building.
ai-error-image-read = The image could not be read. Choose an accessible local file.
ai-error-image-format = The image is damaged or unsupported. Use PNG, JPEG or WebP; export PDF or CAD drawings as an image first.
ai-error-image-size = The image is too large. Use at most 20 MiB, 24 megapixels and 8192 pixels per side; the prepared image must fit within 10 MiB.
ai-error-image-total = Attach up to four images, totalling at most 20 MiB after preparation. Remove an image or reduce its size.
ai-error-vision = The service rejected the image request. Check that the model accepts image_url attachments and supports this request format.
